      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-07-03_WidnesExaminer_art0176" n="art0176">
        <head>TERRITORIAL ROLL OF HONOUR.</head>
        <p>TERRITORIAL ROLL OF HONOUR.</p>
        <p>TWO MORE CASUALTY LISTS THIS WEEK.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-07-03_WidnesExaminer_art0177" n="art0177">
        <head>Killed, 74; Wounded, 362; Missing, 4.</head>
        <p>Killed, 74; Wounded, 362; Missing, 4.</p>
        <p>The .following is an official list of casualties 431 the Warrington Territorids for the week •ending June 26th, issued on Thursday afternoon a headquarters, the Drill Hall, Warrington</p>
        <p>KILLED IN ACTION. 2223 Private W. Hinds, 55, Brick-street, on June 22nd.</p>
        <p>WOUNDED.</p>
        <p>, 2095 !Sergeant H. - - Creamer, 180, WeMeld- street, on June 22nd. 1815 Private T. Hoyles, 3, Canal-street, tarlestown, on June 22nd. 2286 Private R. J. Bleasedale, 33, Dudley- Orett, on June 25th.</p>
        <p>11EPORTED AS MISSING, NOW REPORTED</p>
        <p>WOUNDED.</p>
        <p>The following, who were reported as missing fter the engagement on June 16th, are not in- Ouded in the list of wounded Private W. Rowlands, 26, School Brow. 1463 Private E. Houlston, 3, Bond-street.</p>
        <p>WOUNDED.</p>
        <p>1913 Private C. Littler, 45, Birchall-street, War- rington. 1807 Private F. Hunt, 103, Sharp-street, War- rington. 1726 Private P. Dakin, 15a, Nora-street, War- rington. 254 Lance-Sergeant R. Caslin, 6, Cumberland- street, Warrington.</p>
        <p>REPORTED AS MISSING; NOW REPORTED</p>
        <p>WOUNDED.</p>
        <p>The following, who were reported as missing in the action of June 16th, are now reported wounded:—</p>
        <p>1172 Private J. Lowe, 177, lAwely-lane, War- rington,</p>
        <p>2256 Private H. Stockton, 1, Hale-street, War- rington.</p>
        <p>2337 .Private W. Rothwell, 23, Longford-street, Warrington.</p>
        <p>2051 Private R. Leigh, 43, Forster-street, War- rington. _ _</p>
        <p>2618 Private T. Kimblin, 3, Stamford-yard, Warrington.</p>
        <p>1689 Private S. Massey, 63; Orford-lane, War- rington.</p>
        <p>REPORTED KILLED; NOW • REPORTED</p>
        <p>WOUNDED. The following, previously reported killed, are now reported as having been wounded:- 2226 Private J. T. Taylor, 13, Naylor-street, Warrington. 2050 Private J. Bond, 5, Worrall's-row, War- rington.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-07-03_WidnesExaminer_art0178" n="art0178">
        <head>SUNDAY BATILE.</head>
        <p>A SUNDAY BATILE.</p>
        <p>Three More Killed and Four More Wounded:</p>
        <p>A. 'further list of casualties was issued from -the brill Hall at noon yesterday. It contained the names of those who suffered in fighting took place on Sunday, June 27th, thus iSpelling the rumour that after the heavy losses suffered by the Territorials in the recent great charge they had been taken out of the trenches .for a prolonged spell: Friday's list Ivas as follows:</p>
        <p>KILLED IN ACTION. 1669 Private E. Clare, 23, Neston-street, War-</p>
        <p>1276 Private V. H. Fletcher, 42, Whitefield- l'oad, Stockton Heath. ....2380 Private G. Hart, 4, Eustace-streef, War- .rington.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-07-03_WidnesExaminer_art0179" n="art0179">
        <head>KILLED.</head>
        <p>KILLED.</p>
        <p>PRIVATE V. H. FLETCHER.</p>
        <p>Untinich Death Of Young Man With</p>
        <p>Many Friends.</p>
        <p>Private Victor Henry Fletcher, son of the anaging Director of the Stockton Heath Spade i"rks, was killed in action on Sunday. The I°Ss of Private Fletcher will be keenly felt by tuanY people, as he was of a disposition that</p>
