        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. WAR FUNDS. The Watch Committee have received several complaints of collections being made in the streets of Moneys for the War Funds by un- authorised persons, and in order to prevent the. misapplication of moneys so collected, I am directed to request the Inhabitants of the Borough not to contribute to any collection made on behalf of any War Fund unless the person collecting produces on request an authority to collect signed by the Chief Con- stable on behalf of the Watch Committee. All persons desirous of collecting moneys on behalf of any War Fund are requested to apply to the Chief Constable for the authority of the Watch Committee to do so, which Will only be granted on proof, of the bona-fides of the appli- cant. School children are forbidden to sell articles or to -make promiscuous collections ill: flu streets. Dated this 2nd day of July-, 1915. By order of the Watch Committee, J. LYON WHITTLE. Town Clerk.</p>
