        <p>PRIVATE JOHN. BOOTH, 106, Algernon-street, was crushed through the trench being blown in. He was 21 years of age on the 9th inst. Is a printer at Messrs. Hardi- loan's. Formerly played for Orford St.- John's F.C. PRIVATE JAMES YATES. ' Writes That He Is ," In The Best Of Health." , Private James Yates, who lives at Elizabeth- atreet, has written home to say that he was Irounded in the thigh with shrapnel on the 15th "Doe. not upset yourself," he added, "for am in the best of health, apart from the pain which the wound causes me." Ile is at present in Netley Hospital. Private Yates, who is in A Company, has been ollt the Old Volunteers and Territorials for eight 1,1,.11ine years. He was formerly employed in the ire Ropery at the Whitecross Co.'s works. He educated at St. Barnabas' School, and hqiende the Buckley-street Chapel. He formerly vri°nged to the 'Warrington .P.S.A. ' and had (In several prizes for regular attendance.</p>
