        <p>from a letter written by the gallant Territorial to the Rev. Father Basil Primavesi, in which he gave a graphic descgiption of the "Terriers'" memorable and very gallant charge. Writing subsequently to his brother in Elaine-street, he made further reference to the charge, and said that what with killed, wounded and missing it had cost the "Terriers" something like 250 men. "Those of us," he added, "who came through it will never forget the date, Wednes- day, June 16th. The sights that I saw were horrible; too horrible to describe! . . . .</p>
