        <p>On September 11th, 1905, Mr. T. Rigb, of 121, Church-street, Warrington, said:— "Through having to work out in all weathers I became subject to kidney trouble. For several years I was a sufferer from acute pains in my back, which were sometimes so bad that I could scarcely get about. I was almost afraid to stoop, for it was a difficult matter to straighten myself up again. "For three years 41 took different medi- cines, but -with no good results. It was different, however, when I started with Doan's Backache Kidney Pills; they did me good from the first, and brought me back to health. lam thankful for the benelt Is derived from Doan's Pills, and shall do all I can to make them wider known. • (Signed) "T. RIGBY." On November 21st, 1913—over eight years later—Mr. Rigby said:--" I still keep very well indeed. I have often recommended Doan's Pills. They have done me lasting good." ' Do:4N .BACKANE DOAN'S KL°l4VlPitis PILLS. All dealers, or 219 a box, 6 boxes 1519; from Foster- McClellan Co., 3, Irells-st., Oxford-it., London, Ff. Be sure you get the same Pills as Mr. Rigby had.</p>
